{
  "name": "Daily Appointment Summary",
  "description": "8am CT Mon-Sat: one iMessage brief for Aidan with today's booked calls plus the Respark text-campaign debrief (fresh leads to call first, interested leads, handoffs, new replies, stops, totals).",
  "trigger": {
    "condition": null,
    "config": {
      "trigger_type": "scheduled",
      "events": [],
      "schedule_mode": "recurring",
      "cron_expression": "0 8 * * 1-6",
      "one_time_date": null,
      "timezone": "America/Chicago",
      "interval_value": null,
      "interval_unit": null,
      "interval_anchor": null,
      "ends_type": "never",
      "ends_on_date": null,
      "ends_after_count": null
    }
  },
  "definition": {
    "document": {
      "dsl": "1.0.0",
      "name": "daily_appointment_summary",
      "version": "1.2",
      "namespace": "base44"
    },
    "do": [
      {
        "send_summary": {
          "call": "invoke_backend_function",
          "with": {
            "function_name": "sendAppointmentSummary"
          },
          "then": "respark_report",
          "x-base44": {
            "title": "Count today's appointments",
            "description": "Outlook calendar"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "respark_report": {
          "call": "invoke_backend_function",
          "with": {
            "function_name": "resparkReport",
            "args": {
              "hours": 24
            }
          },
          "then": "brief_aidan",
          "x-base44": {
            "title": "Pull Respark campaign snapshot",
            "description": "Last 24h + fresh leads"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "brief_aidan": {
          "call": "invoke_superagent_step",
          "with": {
            "message": "Morning brief for Aidan. Send ONE plain-text iMessage (no markdown) with two parts.\n\nPART 1, APPOINTMENTS. Result: ${ .send_summary }\nIf today_count is 0, remind Aidan he needs to book 3-5 appointments today from the calling list. If yesterday_count > 0, remind him to mark show/no-show in GHL.\n\nPART 2, RESPARK TEXT CAMPAIGN DEBRIEF. Data: ${ .respark_report }\nCover, briefly and by name with phone number:\n- CALL FIRST: fresh_leads_last_48h. These are brand-new vendor leads (speed-to-lead: a call inside the first hours is worth more than anything else). For each: name, phone, how many hours old, state, driver type, beneficiary, whether they replied yet, and how many call attempts are logged. Tell Aidan to double-dial any with zero attempts before he does anything else.\n- Booked calls (time, confirmed or not, invite status). Flag any ASAP bookings (\"call in 15\") that are still pending.\n- Who is interested / mid-conversation (conversing): what they said, where it stands, what Aidan should do (call them, let the bot keep working, etc.). Pull out anything important a human should know (health, family situation, money objections, divorce, wrong person, hostile).\n- Handoffs waiting on Aidan.\n- Replies in the last 24h that are new.\n- Stops in the last 24h and why (STOP, not interested, wrong number). Note any lead who got the one honest push-back after a first \"no\" and has not answered yet.\n- One line of totals: enrolled, texts sent, reply rate, active.\nSkip empty sections. Keep it tight: this is a text message, not a report. If a lead asked for a call or is clearly interested and not yet booked, lead with that (after the CALL FIRST list)."
          },
          "then": "end",
          "x-base44": {
            "title": "Write and send the iMessage brief",
            "description": "Fresh leads first, then booked, interested, stops"
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}